        <body>
            <div xml:id="d59">

                <pb facs="0161" n="67" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg67"/>

                <head>No. 59.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Trail to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Rio
                                de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-05-04"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 4, 1887</date>.
                        (Received June 4.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 84.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: On May 1 the following cable was received
                    from you: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Trail</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Chargé, Rio:</hi><lb/>President expresses
                            solicitude for health of Emperor.</p>
                        <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                    >Bayard.</hi></p></quote></p>
                <p>On the same day I delivered the message to the Emperor’s chamberlain, and to-day
                    am in receipt of the following reply by telegraph: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p rendition="#right">Rio, <hi rendition="#italic">Maio</hi> 4.</p>
                        <p rendition="#flush">Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Trail</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires, États-Unis Amérique:</hi></p>
                        <p>Sa Majesté Empereur m’ordonne vous prier vouloir bien transmettre S. E.
                            Mr. Président, États-Unis Amérique les remercîments bien vifs pour les
                            voeux exprimés par votre entremise pour le rétablissement santé. Sa
                            Majesté se trouve mieux. Agréez compliments.</p>
                        <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">comte
                                d’aljésur</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Chambellan
                            Semaine.</hi></p></quote></p>
                <p>Which was transmitted you by cable, same date, epitomized in this wise: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bayard</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington:</hi><lb/>Emperor thanks President;
                            is improving.</p>
                        <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                    >Trail.</hi></p></quote></p>
                <p>I have only to add that the court physicians last week moved His Majesty for the
                    third time and that his condition is generally regarded as far from reassuring,
                    light attacks of fever and vomiting recurring at shorter intervals, with
                    increasing feebleness.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles B. Trail</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Chargé.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
